docker-compose build

docker-compose up


Prerequisites
Python 3.6 or later
pip (Python package installer)
Installation
1. Clone the Repository
First, clone the repository to your local machine using git:

git clone https://github.com/SwipeSwipeTeam/product-recsys-api.git
cd product-recsys-api
2. Set Up a Python Virtual Environment
It is recommended to use a virtual environment to manage dependencies. You can set up a virtual environment using venv:

python3 -m venv venv
3. Activate the Virtual Environment
Activate the virtual environment using the following command:

Windows:

venv\Scripts\activate
Mac:

source venv/bin/activate
4. Install the Required Packages
Install the necessary packages from requirements.txt:

pip install -r requirements.txt
5. Usage
To run the project, simply execute the following command:

python3 run.py
Branching rules
Feature branches: For new features, create a branch using the format feature/<jira#>-. For example:

git checkout -b feature/1234-add-login
Bugfix branches: For bug fixes, create a branch using the format bugfix/<jira#>-. For example:

git checkout -b bugfix/1234-add-login
Please create a PR prior to merging into deveop
